  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feed the Future NAFAKA II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tanzania):  &amp;amp;amp;amp;amp;lt;!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--&amp;amp;amp;amp;amp;gt;&amp;amp;lt;!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--&amp;amp;gt;&amp;lt;!--td {border: 1px solid #ccc;}br {mso-data-placement:same-cell;}--&amp;gt;..Feed the Future&apos;s NAFAKA II activity will continue to develop efficient market systems serving rice and maize producers and improving competitiveness and inclusiveness of women and youth. FY 2019 funding will scale-up successful technologies and increase the number of women and youth farmers in the rice and maize market systems. Interventions will concentrate on building small and medium value chain actors&apos; capacity to operate more efficiently, shorten supply chains from producers to markets, and ultimately create more opportunities for small-scale farmers. NAFAKA II will also work with producer associations to develop their financial management systems and create opportunities for volume purchases and sales. NAFAKA II will continue to foster key linkages with other Feed the Future partners involved in fortification, processor operational capacity-building, and on-farm storage. Interventions under this activity align with U.S government priorities to create a more sustainable Tanzania by strengthening the capacity of the country&apos;s agriculture sector to deliver services effectively and efficiently; adopting and implementing policies that lead to inclusive, market-based development; and, ensuring local organizations have the capacity and management systems necessary to lead their own development initiatives...</narrative>
  </description>
